(D3: Discrepancy 3 - `Seek ... to line N` used to land on line 2 for EVERY
 N of 2 or more, and a line target past EOF did not set the error flag
 (LANGUAGE.md:3925, 3927-3928 in manual 0.4.8; the ledger cites the 0.4.7
 numbering 3507, 3509).
 **RESOLVED - fixed by vox #47 (0.4.8).** Re-run against current main, each
 seek lands on the line asked for and the past-EOF target raises the flag.
 The file is AA / BBBB / CCCCCC / DD / EEEEEEEE, five lines of distinct
 lengths, so the landing line is unambiguous; `Read line` keeps the
 trailing newline, which is where the blank lines in the block below come
 from. After the failed seek to line 99 the read returns nothing.
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/D3.vox -o p && ./p
 actual output:
   line 1 -> AA

   line 2 -> BBBB

   line 3 -> CCCCCC

   line 5 -> EEEEEEEE

   seek to line 99 past EOF set the error flag
   line 99 ->
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/files".
open a file for writing called seedfile at "vf_scratch/files/five.txt".
Write "AA\nBBBB\nCCCCCC\nDD\nEEEEEEEE\n" to seedfile.
Close seedfile.
open a file for reading called 'the first reader' at "vf_scratch/files/five.txt".
a buffer called 'the first line' is 32 bytes in size.
Seek 'the first reader' to line 1.
Read line from 'the first reader' into 'the first line'.
print "line 1 -> {'the first line'}".
Close 'the first reader'.
open a file for reading called 'the second reader' at "vf_scratch/files/five.txt".
a buffer called 'the second line' is 32 bytes in size.
Seek 'the second reader' to line 2.
Read line from 'the second reader' into 'the second line'.
print "line 2 -> {'the second line'}".
Close 'the second reader'.
open a file for reading called 'the third reader' at "vf_scratch/files/five.txt".
a buffer called 'the third line' is 32 bytes in size.
Seek 'the third reader' to line 3.
On error print "seek to line 3 set the error flag".
Read line from 'the third reader' into 'the third line'.
print "line 3 -> {'the third line'}".
Close 'the third reader'.
open a file for reading called 'the fifth reader' at "vf_scratch/files/five.txt".
a buffer called 'the fifth line' is 32 bytes in size.
Seek 'the fifth reader' to line 5.
On error print "seek to line 5 set the error flag".
Read line from 'the fifth reader' into 'the fifth line'.
print "line 5 -> {'the fifth line'}".
Close 'the fifth reader'.
open a file for reading called 'the far reader' at "vf_scratch/files/five.txt".
a buffer called 'the far line' is 32 bytes in size.
Seek 'the far reader' to line 99.
On error print "seek to line 99 past EOF set the error flag".
Read line from 'the far reader' into 'the far line'.
print "line 99 -> {'the far line'}".
Close 'the far reader'.
